  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1211 PM EST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nEarly afternoon GOES satellite imagery reveals mostly clear skies \noverhead the UP and Lake Superior save for some areas of high cirrus \nand SW lake effect cu in the northwestern lake under localized \nridging. Temps in the upper 30s to low 40s warm a bit further to the \nmid 40s this afternoon. Weak high pressure sprawling south into the \nlower Midwest gives way to a sharp shortwave that digs across \nOntario down through the Great Lakes tonight through Sunday. The \nresultant sfc low pressure remains well northeast of us, keeping \nsynoptic precip shunted into Canada, but 850 mb temps falling \nbetween -1 to -4C above a +9C Lake superior sfc temp average will be \nenough of a temp differential to produce lake effect rain showers in \nthe east half. Additionally, given the quick uptick in NW flow, \nlight rain showers are possible in the west/central in common \nupslope enhancement zones of the Keweenaw and Michigamme Highlands. \nOverall precip amounts look to remain light, generally a dime at \nmost with isolated dime to quarter amounts in more persistent LE \nrain showers across the far eastern portions of the UP. Pressure \nrises and cold air advection will contribute to gusty NW winds on \nthe rise through much of Sunday. Ensemble guidance suggests a 70-\n100% chance for gales between 35-45 kts across the central and \neastern portions of the lake and gusts 25-40 mph along the shores of \nLake Superior, greatest between Munising and Grand Marias. These \nwinds will act to build significant wave heights along the central \nand eastern UP shorelines between 10-15 ft. Stay dry when waves\nare high!\n\nThe cycle repeats itself early next week. Ridging in the wake of \nthis clipper results in another dry period with lighter winds Monday \nthrough Tuesday morning. The next shortwave in the clipper train \nlooks to arrive Tuesday afternoon, though once again the low looks \ndisplaced too far north and too weak to drive synoptic precipitation \nfor the UP. Colder air in the wake of the clipper will bring lake \neffect precipitation chances (25-60%) that persists through late \nweek as winds turn northerly. Guidance has trended back on gust \npotential, not expecting widespread gusts like tomorrow's forecast. \nTemps return near normal with highs in the mid 30s to low 40s and \nlows in the 20s to low 30s.",
